<title>UK: Four EU green rates to devalue on Saturday - HGCA.</title>
<headline>Four EU green rates to devalue on Saturday - HGCA.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The green rates of the Belgian franc, Dutch guilder, German mark and Austrian schilling will be devalued with effect from Saturday, the UK's Home Grown Cereals Authority (HGCA) said on Friday.</p>
<p>The new rates are 40.4180 per Ecu for the green Belgian franc (old rate 40.3225), 1.95903 for the mark (1.95431), 2.20270 for the guilder (2.19831) and 13.7880 for the Austrian Schilling (13.7529).</p>
<p>Also on Saturday, green sterling will enter the second of five possible confirmation periods ahead of a revaluation on June 5, the HGCA said.</p>
<p>The next monitoring period will be from April 26 to May 5, the HGCA said.</p>
<p>Green rates are used by the European Union (EU) to convert Ecu into the currencies of its member stats in its Common Agricultural Policy. --Christopher Lyddon, London newsroom +44 171 542 7928</p>
